.npmrc
react-library/.npmrc

# Build artifacts that should never go to the upload — they're regenerated on Vercel.
.next
# Forensics + heap snapshots from scripts/next-memory-forensics.js / probe-dev-heap-cap.mjs.
memory-forensics-*
*.heapsnapshot
probe-results.json
# Per-run output of scripts/probe-build-memory.mjs.
/.build-memory

# Tester plugin submodule — dev tooling only, never part of the app build.
# It carries @playwright/mcp + its own node_modules; shipping it inflates the
# upload, and an oversized bundle fails Vercel's "Deploying outputs..." step
# (CLAUDE.md Recurrent Root Cause #6).
#
# 🛑 The leading slash is load-bearing. .vercelignore uses gitignore semantics,
# so a bare `tester` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth — which also
# matched `src/app/[locale]/user/tester/`, stripping the Tester Hub page from
# the upload. The build then had no such route and /user/tester returned a hard
# 404 in production (X-Matched-Path: /404) while the page sat committed in the
# repo since 2026-08-17, so nothing local could reproduce it. Anchor every
# pattern here that names a root-level path.
/tester

# appkit source submodule — 2,359 files / 356 KLOC plus a 27 MB dist/ and its own
# node_modules, uploaded on every deploy for no reason. package.json pins
# "@mohasinac/appkit" to the npm REGISTRY, so `npm ci` installs the published
# tarball into node_modules and nothing in the build ever reads appkit/ itself:
#   - tsconfig.json deliberately excludes appkit/src/** (Root Cause #23 — it OOMs
#     Vercel's Linux builder), and scripts/deploy.mjs Check 2 enforces that.
#   - next.config.js used to `require("./appkit/package.json")` for a footer
#     version string. That single line was the whole coupling; it now reads the
#     installed copy under node_modules instead.
#
# 🛑 Leading slash, same reason as /tester above — a bare `appkit` would also
# match any nested directory named appkit.
#
# 🛑 If you switch the pin back to "file:./appkit" for local development, this
# line MUST come out or `npm ci` on Vercel has nothing to install from. See
# CLAUDE.md "Appkit Local Dev vs Publish Rules".
/appkit
